  "notes": "Well-visible salmon/terracotta-pink two-storey villa with an orange-red tiled hipped roof; a small tiled entrance-porch canopy projects at the front (modelled as a low 1-floor porch volume). Upper facade has three narrow vertical slit windows; a ground-floor window at right has security bars/grille (bars not expressible in openings). Frontage: very ornate white wrought-iron vehicle+pedestrian gates with a blue '6' house-number plate, a cream stone-block low wall and a brown wood picket fence to the right (#9a6a3f). Colours sampled from ref 2026-07-04. Environment (2026-07-05): tall date palm dominating the yard, a low round shrub at left, a young sapling by the pedestrian gate, spiky yucca/agave grass clumps in a raised bed at the foreground, and a green wheelie bin behind the gate; no parked cars visible."
